c_compute_round_and_revert()` [GPU kernel]\n   - **D2H copy**: `copy_from_device()` within `observe_and_update()` at line 955 (for precompute-M) or via `reconstruct_s_evals()` → `d_sum_evals.to_host()` at line 1132\n\n2. **Subsequent sumcheck rounds** (lines 713-1055):\n   - **Strategy Selection** (line 680): Chooses between two backends:\n   \n   **a) FoldEval Strategy** (lines 718-820):\n   - Loop over xi_prev (line 721): `for &xi_j in xi_prev.iter().skip(1)`\n   - For each iteration:\n     - Call `do_fused_sumcheck_round()` or `do_fused_sumcheck_round_inplace()`\n     - Each calls GPU kernel: `frac_compute_round_and_fold()` or `frac_compute_round_and_fold_inplace()`\n     - **D2H copy per iteration**: `observe_and_update()` → `reconstruct_s_evals()` → `d_sum_evals.to_host()` at line 1132\n   - After loop, final fold with `fold_ef_frac_columns_inplace()`\n   \n   **CRITICAL INEFFICIENCY HERE**: If round has k sumcheck rounds, you get k D2H copies of 2 EF values each. Example: round 5 means 5 sumcheck rounds = 5 D2H transfers per GKR round.\n\n   **b) PrecomputeM Strategy** (lines 821-1054):\n   - Window-based processing of w=3 variables per window\n   - **M-build** (lines 910-926): GPU kernel `frac_precompute_m_build_raw()`\n   - **Window eval loop** (lines 929-966):\n     ```\n     for t in 0..w:\n       - H2D: copy_to_device_ptr(eq_r_prefix_buffer, ...)  [line 936]\n       - H2D: copy_to_device_ptr(eq_suffix_buffer, ...)    [line 940]\n       - GPU: frac_precompute_m_eval_round_raw()            [line 944]\n       - D2H: observe_and_update() → to_host()             [line 955]\n     ```\n   - **Multifold** (lines 988-996): GPU kernel `frac_multifold_raw()`\n   - **Tail rounds** (lines 1002-1046): Fall back to fold-eval for remaining rounds\n\n3. **End of GKR round** (lines 1057-1078):\n   - **D2H copies of pq_host**: Lines 1058-1059\n     ```rust\n     copy_from_device(active, 0, &mut copy_scratch)?\n     copy_from_device(active, pq_size / 2, &mut copy_scratch)?\n     ```\n   - Observe 4 values in transcript, sample mu\n   - Store claims for next round\n\n#### Key GPU Kernel Summary\n\n**CUDA Files**:\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr.cu` (1452 lines)\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.cu`\n\n**Main Kernels**:\n1. `frac_build_tree_layer_kernel` - Tree layer aggregation (with optional alpha, with revert)\n2. `frac_build_tree_two_layers_kernel` - Fused two-layer build\n3. `frac_compute_round_and_revert_kernel` - Sumcheck + revert (first inner round)\n4. `frac_compute_round_and_fold_kernel` - Sumcheck + fold (out-of-place, ping-pong)\n5. `frac_compute_round_and_fold_inplace_kernel` - Sumcheck + fold (in-place)\n6. `precompute_m_build_partial_kernel` - M-matrix partial building\n7. `precompute_m_eval_round_kernel` - Extract s'(1), s'(2) from M\n8. `frac_multifold_kernel` - Multi-coordinate fold\n\n### Critical Synchronization Points and Bottlenecks\n\n#### 1. **Per-AIR Sequential Processing in Input Evaluation** (Line 108)\n- **Issue**: The `for meta in trace_interactions.iter().flatten()` loop processes AIRs sequentially\n- **Impact**: With APC=300, you have ~300 sequential logup_gkr_input_eval kernel launches\n- **Opportunity**: Batch across multiple AIRs instead of one-at-a-time. Could group kernel launches or consolidate into fewer, wider kernels\n\n#### 2. **D2H Copies in Each GKR Round** (Line 1132, 1058-1059)\n- **FoldEval Strategy**: \n  - Per-round cost: (num_sumcheck_rounds) × D2H(2 EF values)\n  - For round j: j-1 inner rounds = j-1 D2H copies\n  - Total across all rounds: sum(j for j in 1..n) = O(n²) D2H transfers\n  \n- **PrecomputeM Strategy** (Lines 955, 1058-1059):\n  - M-eval loop: w D2H copies per window (lines 956 at each iteration)\n  - End-of-round: 2 D2H copies (lines 1058-1059)\n  - Tail rounds: fall back to fold-eval D2H\n\n#### 3. **H2D Copies in PrecomputeM** (Lines 936, 940, 974, 978)\n- **M-eval loop**: 2 H2D per window round (lines 936, 940)\n- **Multifold setup**: 1 H2D for eq_r_window (lines 974 or 978)\n- **Impact**: Small buffers (2^w ≈ 8-16 elements) but high frequency\n\n#### 4. **Missing Batching Across GKR Rounds**\n- Each GKR round (j = 1..n) is independent of previous rounds in terms of GPU computation\n- However, they process sequentially due to D2H copies blocking for transcript sampling\n- **Opportunity**: Could potentially start GPU kernels for multiple rounds asynchronously\n\n### Data Flow Summary\n\n```\nlog_gkr_input_evals()                      [H2D: main, preprocessed, rules]\n  └─> For each AIR:\n        └─> logup_gkr_input_eval (GPU)      [produces: 2^n leaves (p, q) pairs]\n            If height < lifted_height:\n              └─> frac_matrix_vertically_repeat (GPU)\n\nfractional_sumcheck_gpu()\n  ├─> Bit-reverse + Tree build              [GPU: all leaves → root]\n  │   └─> D2H: root (2 EF values)\n  │\n  └─> For each GKR round j:\n        ├─> Revert layer j                   [GPU]\n        │\n        ├─> For each sumcheck round:\n        │   ├─> (PrecomputeM) H2D: eq_r_prefix, eq_suffix\n        │   ├─> (PrecomputeM) GPU: M-build, M-eval\n        │   ├─> GPU: compute_round\n        │   └─> D2H: s'(1), s'(2)            [2 EF values per inner round]\n        │\n        ├─> D2H: pq_buffer[0], pq_buffer[size/2]  [4 values for next round claims]\n        └─> Observe in transcript, sample challenges\n```\n\n### Loop Structure Summary\n\n**AIR Loop**: Sequential, **not batched**\n- 1 loop iteration per AIR with interactions\n- Each iteration: independent kernel calls\n\n**GKR Round Loop**: Sequential, **data dependencies**\n- `for round in 1..total_rounds` (typically total_rounds = l_skip + n_logup ≈ 20-30)\n- Each round depends on previous D2H values for challenge sampling\n\n**Sumcheck Inner Rounds**: Sequential, **blocking on D2H**\n- FoldEval: `for &xi_j in xi_prev.iter().skip(1)`\n- PrecomputeM: `for t in 0..w`\n- Each iteration performs D2H copy → CPU processing → sample challenge\n\n### Obvious Inefficiencies\n\n1. **Sequential per-AIR input evaluation** (300+ calls for APC=300)\n   - Could batch into fewer kernel launches\n   - No explicit stream usage to overlap\n\n2. **Small, frequent D2H copies**\n   - Each D2H: only 2-4 EF values (16-32 bytes for BN254)\n   - Frequency: O(n²) where n ≈ 20-30, so ~400-900 D2H transfers\n   - Could batch transcript observations\n\n3. **Blocking H2D/D2H in precompute-M window loop**\n   - Lines 935-942: H2D per window round\n   - Line 955 (via observe_and_update): D2H per window round\n   - Lines 974/978: H2D per window (before multifold)\n   - Could batch all H2D transfers and pipeline kernels\n\n4. **No multi-stream pipelining visible**\n   - GKR input eval kernels appear async, but no explicit stream coordination\n   - GKR rounds sequential due to transcript sampling dependencies\n\n5. **Tree revert synchronization**\n   - FoldEval strategy must preserve layer buffer (lines 795-819)\n   - Creates ping-pong between layer and work_buffer\n   - Non-last rounds stay in work_buffer to preserve layer for reverts\n\n### Expected ~808ms Breakdown (Hypothesis)\n\n- GKR input eval (300 AIRs): ~300ms (300 kernel calls, partially overlappable)\n- Segment tree build: ~50ms (bit-reversal + log₂(2^{l_skip+n_logup}) layers)\n- GKR rounds (20-30 rounds): ~400ms\n  - Per round: ~12-20ms for kernels\n  - D2H latency & CPU overhead: ~2-5ms per round\n- H2D/D2H in precompute-M: ~30ms total (small but frequent)\n\n---\n\n## Recommendations for Optimization\n\n1. **Batch AIR input evaluations**: Merge multiple AIRs into single kernel or use multiple streams\n2. **Batch D2H copies**: Collect 4-8 rounds worth of data before transferring to reduce overhead\n3. **Eliminate redundant H2D in precompute-M**: Compute eq_r_prefix/suffix on GPU instead\n4. **Multi-stream pipeline**: Use separate streams for concurrent GKR rounds if challenge sampling allows\n5. **Fuse transcript operations**: Reduce