arallelism opportunities.\n\nNow I'm breaking down the actual wall clock timing more carefully: the GKR input eval is 428ms of GPU kernel time but probably takes 450-500ms wall clock when accounting for sync overhead, while the fractional sumcheck's 244ms GPU time translates to roughly 308-358ms wall clock due to heavier synchronization costs from the data dependencies. This suggests the input eval optimization is the higher-leverage target.\n\nLet me dive into the GKR input eval code to understand how to apply multi-streaming there.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1557,"cache_read_input_tokens":68866,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1557},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93785c5e-49ce-4ca5-bdce-28569746575a","uuid":"f19fcbe3-57bd-4d37-9e47-239531c04301"}
