{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_017vXKPR37YAE8JhASuyh6iY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012udEAs7vEeoK1xDdW9SHJW","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-13-0115-multistream-gkr-input-eval\n\nParallelize the LogUp GKR input evaluation across multiple OS threads with per-thread CUDA streams, using the same multi-stream pattern that achieved 1.89x improvement on Round 0. Nsight profiling shows 791 sequential per-AIR kernel launches (428ms total GPU time) in `log_gkr_input_evals()`, each using only 1-4 SMs on the RTX 4090's 128 SMs. By distributing these independent per-AIR evaluations across 4 threads (each with its own `cudaStreamPerThread`), kernels from different threads can execute concurrently on idle SMs, reducing the GKR input eval wall clock from ~450ms to ~180-220ms and LogUp GKR from 808ms to ~560-630ms.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1571,"cache_read_input_tokens":93782,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1571},"output_tokens":65,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93785c5e-49ce-4ca5-bdce-28569746575a","uuid":"0227dd54-563e-4b8b-b639-ccc40ea4c506"}
