{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SMZJGGirb3D5HKbLMrEDgt","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-13-0115-multistream-gkr-input-eval\n2\t\n3\tParallelize the LogUp GKR input evaluation across multiple OS threads with per-thread CUDA streams, using the same multi-stream pattern that achieved 1.89x improvement on Round 0. Nsight profiling shows 791 sequential per-AIR kernel launches (428ms total GPU time) in `log_gkr_input_evals()`, each using only 1-4 SMs on the RTX 4090's 128 SMs. By distributing these independent per-AIR evaluations across 4 threads (each with its own `cudaStreamPerThread`), kernels from different threads can execute concurrently on idle SMs, reducing the GKR input eval wall clock from ~450ms to ~180-220ms and LogUp GKR from 808ms to ~560-630ms.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01By1tEchMnHokaJtgTou8T2","session_id":"93785c5e-49ce-4ca5-bdce-28569746575a","uuid":"fa5a2472-2a07-4a4a-b006-2752df52930e","timestamp":"2026-04-12T23:19:23.404Z"}
